## Rotating Card – CSS + HTML

Below is a minimal, self‑contained example that shows a card (a `<div>` with some content) that rotates around the Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy‑paste the code into an `.html` file and open it in a browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card on Hover</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣  Container ---------- */
.card-wrapper {
  perspective: 1000px;          /* gives depth to the 3D effect */
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  margin: 50px auto;
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣  The Card ---------- */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  background: #fff;
  border-radius: 12px;
  box-shadow: 0 10px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
  transition: transform 0.6s ease;   /* smooth rotation */
  transform-style: preserve-3d;      /* keep children in 3D space */
  cursor: pointer;
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣  Front & Back Faces ---------- */
.card .face {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden;      /* hide the back side when turned */
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  color: #333;
  border-radius: 12px;
}

.card .front {
  background: #f8f9fa;
}

.card .back {
  background: #e9ecef;
  transform: rotateY(180deg);       /* place it behind the front */
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣  Hover Effect ---------- */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);        /* flip the card on hover */
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="face front">
      <p>Front Side</p>
    </div>
    <div class="face back">
      <p>Back Side</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens |
|------|--------------|
| **1** | `perspective` on the wrapper creates a 3‑D space. |
| **2** | The `.card` element is the rotating object. |
| **3** | Two faces (`.front` and `.back`) are positioned absolutely. The back face is rotated 180° so it sits behind the front. |
| **4** | On hover, the card itself rotates 180° around the Y‑axis, revealing the back face. |

#### Tweaks you can try

| Property | What to change | Result |
|----------|----------------|--------|
| `transform: rotateY(180deg)` | Use `rotateX(180deg)` for a vertical flip. | Card flips up/down instead of left/right. |
| `transition: transform 0.6s ease` | Adjust the duration or easing. | Faster/slower or different animation feel. |
| `perspective: 800px` | Lower value → more pronounced 3‑D effect. | Card looks more “deep”. |
| `background` colors | Use gradients or images. | Custom card design. |

Enjoy experimenting!
